      "composition": "single-ornament",
      "description": "A wide, symmetrical etched cartouche frieze. The centre is an open blank field bounded by leafy scrolls, with a bearded mask at the top and a knot of leaves at the bottom. To each side a horned, winged female hybrid whose lower body turns into acanthus scroll leans toward the field, a cluster of grapes hanging beside her; at either end a bear bites the scaly dragon-headed terminal of the outer volute, and the frieze ends in fish-scaled curls. Dark brown ink on a transparent background; the faint paper tone of the plate is kept at low opacity, and the title lettering in the field was removed.",
